WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:01.492
It's school choice week.

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:02.940
But what does school choice

00:00:02.940 --> 00:00:03.860
mean?

00:00:03.860 --> 00:00:05.500
How do we spell the sun

00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:06.660
that's outside?

00:00:06.660 --> 00:00:08.340
S-U-N.

00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:09.063
It might mean

00:00:09.063 --> 00:00:10.360
schools where kids

00:00:10.360 --> 00:00:11.640
like learning.

00:00:11.640 --> 00:00:12.840
Learning is work.

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:14.040
It don't matter.

00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:16.113
These kids, or rather their parents

00:00:16.113 --> 00:00:18.067
chose a different kind of school,

00:00:18.067 --> 00:00:19.280
a charter school.

00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:20.800
That's a public school,

00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:22.080
but one outside the

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:24.300
normal government bureaucracy.

00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:27.160
Kids at these Success Academy charters

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:28.740
do remarkably well.

00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:29.960
We are number one

00:00:29.960 --> 00:00:31.215
in student achievement

00:00:31.215 --> 00:00:32.700
in the state of New York.

00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:34.300
We're outperforming

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:35.981
all of the wealthy suburbs.

00:00:35.981 --> 00:00:37.920
Success Academy teaches mostly

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:38.940
poor kids,

00:00:38.940 --> 00:00:40.120
but 95 percent

00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:41.920
passed the state math test,

00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:44.320
84 percent the English test.

00:00:44.320 --> 00:00:45.773
Government-run schools

00:00:45.773 --> 00:00:47.623
have a much lower pass rate.

00:00:47.623 --> 00:00:48.680
How does Success

00:00:48.690 --> 00:00:49.760
do it?

00:00:49.760 --> 00:00:51.360
You keep them in school longer.

00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:55.140
Our instructional day starts at 7:45,

00:00:55.140 --> 00:00:57.260
middle schoolers go till 4:30.

00:00:57.260 --> 00:00:58.320
Open up your book,

00:00:58.320 --> 00:00:59.480
you should be sitting up straight.

00:00:59.480 --> 00:01:01.280
This is too hard on the kids,

00:01:01.280 --> 00:01:02.320
it's stressful.

00:01:02.320 --> 00:01:03.600
China and India are not

00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:05.000
worrying about

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:06.800
the length of the school day.

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:08.340
We have to toughen up a little bit.

00:01:08.340 --> 00:01:09.760
Reading is work

00:01:09.760 --> 00:01:11.900
but it's rockin' awesome.

00:01:11.900 --> 00:01:13.040
I think I've read each year

00:01:13.040 --> 00:01:14.300
I've read 100 books.

00:01:14.300 --> 00:01:15.460
Our level of rigor is

00:01:15.460 --> 00:01:18.260
much higher than in most district schools.

00:01:18.260 --> 00:01:20.440
Just more rigor works?

00:01:20.440 --> 00:01:21.071
It does.

00:01:21.071 --> 00:01:23.120
Kids rise to your level of

00:01:23.130 --> 00:01:24.330
expectation.

00:01:24.330 --> 00:01:26.660
Good morning kindergarten scholars.

00:01:26.660 --> 00:01:29.680
Good morning Miss Neptune.

00:01:29.680 --> 00:01:31.880
And even though the kids work hard,

00:01:31.880 --> 00:01:32.860
somehow

00:01:32.860 --> 00:01:34.080
they like the work.

00:01:34.080 --> 00:01:34.920
School

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:35.980
is boring.

00:01:35.980 --> 00:01:38.240
No it's not.

00:01:38.240 --> 00:01:39.000
They told me,

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:40.560
learning is fun.

00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:42.280
How is it fun to learn?

00:01:42.280 --> 00:01:44.700
They just teach us in a fun way.

00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:46.920
I was surprised that the kids seemed

00:01:46.920 --> 00:01:47.720
happy.

00:01:47.720 --> 00:01:48.900
How could kids

00:01:48.900 --> 00:01:49.400
like

00:01:49.400 --> 00:01:50.500
work?

00:01:50.500 --> 00:01:51.320
It's hard.

00:01:51.320 --> 00:01:52.440
It's hard,

00:01:52.440 --> 00:01:54.000
but actually

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:55.540
kids like

00:01:55.540 --> 00:01:57.380
succeeding at things.

00:01:57.380 --> 00:01:57.880
So you guys look forward

00:01:57.880 --> 00:02:00.917
to going to school in the morning?

00:02:00.917 --> 00:02:01.417
Yes.

00:02:01.417 --> 00:02:03.118
Yet Eva Moskowitz is hated.

00:02:03.118 --> 00:02:05.170
When she goes to public meetings

00:02:05.170 --> 00:02:07.200
to propose opening a new school,

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:09.060
people scream at her.

00:02:09.060 --> 00:02:10.900
Y'all are not welcome here.

00:02:10.900 --> 00:02:12.640
We will not welcome you here.

00:02:12.640 --> 00:02:14.000
We will fight.

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:17.080
I will fight until my dying day.

00:02:17.080 --> 00:02:18.540
They just hate you.

00:02:18.540 --> 00:02:20.020
They do,

00:02:20.020 --> 00:02:20.880
they do.

00:02:20.880 --> 00:02:23.300
The charter school will not be inside

00:02:23.300 --> 00:02:25.800
of P.S. 194.

00:02:25.800 --> 00:02:26.540
They hate her,

00:02:26.540 --> 00:02:27.220
she says

00:02:27.220 --> 00:02:28.940
because

00:02:28.940 --> 00:02:29.760
what we prove

00:02:29.760 --> 00:02:32.100
is that there's nothing wrong with the children,

00:02:32.100 --> 00:02:34.960
there is something wrong with the system,

00:02:34.960 --> 00:02:36.859
a monopolistic system that is

00:02:36.859 --> 00:02:38.480
not allowing

00:02:38.480 --> 00:02:39.680
kids

00:02:39.680 --> 00:02:41.300
to succeed.

00:02:41.300 --> 00:02:42.540
Time for Eva Moskowitz

00:02:42.540 --> 00:02:44.660
to stop having the run of the place.

00:02:44.660 --> 00:02:46.800
Defenders of the government monopoly

00:02:46.820 --> 00:02:48.040
are everywhere.

00:02:48.040 --> 00:02:50.320
One is commentator Nomiki Konst.

00:02:50.320 --> 00:02:52.160
Reality is, charter schools are better funded

00:02:52.160 --> 00:02:53.640
by these hedge funders

00:02:53.640 --> 00:02:55.600
and they're performing worse than the underfunded

00:02:55.609 --> 00:02:56.109
schools.

00:02:56.109 --> 00:02:57.364
The results are in.

00:02:57.364 --> 00:02:58.105
It's a scam.

00:02:58.105 --> 00:02:59.320
She's just wrong.

00:02:59.320 --> 00:03:00.799
Wrong about the results,

00:03:00.799 --> 00:03:02.759
but what about the funding?

00:03:02.759 --> 00:03:03.780
You have more money.

00:03:03.780 --> 00:03:05.860
You've got billionaires donating.

00:03:05.860 --> 00:03:06.680
Less money.

00:03:06.680 --> 00:03:08.160
So New York spends about

00:03:08.160 --> 00:03:11.222
almost $20,000 dollars per student.

00:03:11.222 --> 00:03:13.609
Yeah and I only get $14,500

00:03:13.609 --> 00:03:15.588
and I'm getting vastly better results.

00:03:15.588 --> 00:03:18.049
You do well because you're a test prep factory.

00:03:18.049 --> 00:03:19.599
You just drill them.

00:03:19.599 --> 00:03:21.314
We do not run schools

00:03:21.320 --> 00:03:22.580
for tests.

00:03:22.580 --> 00:03:24.100
We really believe in games.

00:03:24.100 --> 00:03:26.940
In kindergarten we play Blokus and backgammon,

00:03:26.960 --> 00:03:29.200
second grade we do Monopoly.

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:32.820
We have math teams, robotics teams, debate teams.

00:03:32.820 --> 00:03:34.340
You cherry-pick the kids.

00:03:34.340 --> 00:03:35.400
Simply not true.

00:03:35.400 --> 00:03:37.370
We admit by random lottery.

00:03:37.370 --> 00:03:38.935
Many charters do.

00:03:38.940 --> 00:03:40.080
You see the pages up  here,

00:03:40.080 --> 00:03:41.400
it's a random selection.

00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:42.760
You all have your numbers, right?

00:03:42.760 --> 00:03:44.140
Finally, critics say

00:03:44.140 --> 00:03:46.680
yes, Eva takes kids by lottery

00:03:46.680 --> 00:03:47.565
but then she kicks

00:03:47.565 --> 00:03:49.020
problem kids out.

00:03:49.020 --> 00:03:49.619
You say,

00:03:49.619 --> 00:03:51.940
maybe this school isn't for you.

00:03:51.945 --> 00:03:54.250
Well why would our student

00:03:54.250 --> 00:03:57.084
retention rates be so much higher

00:03:57.084 --> 00:03:58.630
than the district?

00:03:58.630 --> 00:03:59.403
Are they?

00:03:59.403 --> 00:04:00.100
They are.

00:04:00.100 --> 00:04:01.320
Significantly.

00:04:01.320 --> 00:04:04.920
We lose about 10 percent of our families

00:04:04.920 --> 00:04:07.920
every year and the districts lose about 20 percent.

00:04:07.920 --> 00:04:10.240
All reasons parents line up

00:04:10.240 --> 00:04:11.500
hoping to give their kids

00:04:11.500 --> 00:04:12.000
a chance

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:14.660
to escape government-run schools.

00:04:14.660 --> 00:04:15.860
This line

00:04:15.860 --> 00:04:17.280
goes on

00:04:17.280 --> 00:04:18.620
and on.

00:04:18.620 --> 00:04:20.580
Kids whose names are not drawn

00:04:20.580 --> 00:04:21.420
cry.

00:04:21.420 --> 00:04:24.080
Oh it's heartbreaking.

00:04:24.080 --> 00:04:25.580
If you win our lottery,

00:04:25.580 --> 00:04:26.960
you are guaranteed

00:04:26.960 --> 00:04:28.140
as a young child

00:04:28.140 --> 00:04:29.620
to learn how to read.

00:04:29.620 --> 00:04:31.800
Of course not every charter is good.

00:04:31.800 --> 00:04:34.720
Some turn out to be worse than schools they replace.

00:04:34.720 --> 00:04:36.740
But the beauty of choice,

00:04:36.740 --> 00:04:37.580
a market,

00:04:37.580 --> 00:04:39.040
is that bad schools

00:04:39.040 --> 00:04:40.840
gradually disappear

00:04:40.840 --> 00:04:42.680
The good schools grow.

00:04:42.680 --> 00:04:43.480
KIPP

00:04:43.480 --> 00:04:46.220
started a knowledge is power program school

00:04:46.220 --> 00:04:47.860
just 20 years ago.

00:04:47.860 --> 00:04:50.580
Now the chain has 209 schools.

00:04:50.580 --> 00:04:51.960
IDEA has several

00:04:51.960 --> 00:04:54.200
of the top-ranked high schools in the country.

00:04:54.200 --> 00:04:55.570
With 61 schools,

00:04:55.570 --> 00:04:58.180
it's now the fastest-growing charter chain.

00:04:58.180 --> 00:04:59.320
And Eva Moskowitz

00:04:59.320 --> 00:05:00.036
now runs

00:05:00.040 --> 00:05:01.360
46 schools.

00:05:01.360 --> 00:05:03.800
There's work to do on behalf of children

00:05:03.800 --> 00:05:06.060
and I'm going to continue to do that work.

00:05:06.060 --> 00:05:07.315
Eva's the Democrat

00:05:07.315 --> 00:05:08.500
who once believed

00:05:08.500 --> 00:05:10.180
that government-run schools

00:05:10.180 --> 00:05:10.880
were fine.

00:05:10.880 --> 00:05:11.760
She explains that

00:05:11.760 --> 00:05:13.180
in her new book.

00:05:13.180 --> 00:05:14.140
What do you mean

00:05:14.140 --> 00:05:16.240
The education of Eva?

00:05:16.240 --> 00:05:17.440
Were you dumb before?

00:05:17.440 --> 00:05:20.140
Well no, I was not dumb,

00:05:20.140 --> 00:05:21.820
but I was

00:05:21.820 --> 00:05:23.352
blinded I think

00:05:23.360 --> 00:05:24.540
by

00:05:24.540 --> 00:05:25.920
a belief

00:05:25.920 --> 00:05:29.480
that big government was a good thing.

00:05:29.480 --> 00:05:30.680
What do you mean by

00:05:30.680 --> 00:05:32.016
they need freedom?

00:05:32.016 --> 00:05:34.000
Now Eva's been educated,

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:35.100
and her students

00:05:35.100 --> 00:05:37.020
have discussions like this.

00:05:37.027 --> 00:05:39.400
Everybody has a different life

00:05:39.400 --> 00:05:40.770
so they could do

00:05:40.770 --> 00:05:42.800
whatever they want.

00:05:52.800 --> 00:05:54.860
you

